<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tell Leilan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tell Leilan is an archaeological site in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, the remains of an ancient city of upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. Excavations suggest that it was abandoned around the late third millennium BCE. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a> link this abandonment to a severe drought around 2200–2150 BCE that caused crop failures and population displacement, contributing to the empire's decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tell-leilan.jpg" alt="Tell Leilan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zoeperkoe · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tell_Leilan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
